.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH trellis-version-plan 1 "" trellis "Trellis Manual"
.SH NAME
trellis\-version\-plan \- Dry\-run: show what `version apply` would bump
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrellis version plan\fR [\fB\-\-bump\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-pre\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dry\-run: show what `version apply` would bump
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bump\fR \fI<LEVEL|PKG=LEVEL>\fR
Override the derived bump level, workspace\-wide (`\-\-bump major`) or for one package (`\-\-bump lat_core=major`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run as if started in this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<PKG=VERSION>\fR
Pin a package\*(Aqs next version exactly (`\-\-set lat_core=1.0.0`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-pre\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Cut a prerelease: `\-\-pre rc` gives 1.0.0\-rc.1, and again 1.0.0\-rc.2. Fragments stay unreleased until the final version. `\-\-pre none` promotes the current prerelease to its final version and consumes them
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
